      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $4+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}$ for $x>0$.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(4+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(4+\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= 4\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= 4\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+\\frac{x^{-\\frac{3}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+C \\\\ &= 4x-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
